            <ArticleTitle>CT scanography for limb length determination.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>267-74</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present an alternative to classic techniques used to measure limb length discrepancy radiographically. CT scanography seems to have advantages over currently-used Bell-Thompson roentgenography in that it uses less radiation and is of no increase in cost.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
